# Spider-Verse: "Whenever you cast a spell from anywhere other than your hand, you may copy it. If you do, you may choose new targets for the
# copy. If the copy is a permanent spell, it gains haste. Do this only once each turn." Wrenn's Resolve exiles two Grizzly Bears, played from
# exile on turn five: the first is copied (the token has haste, and so can attack at once; the Bears that was cast cannot), and the second,
# cast the same turn, neither triggers nor asks, as the allowance is spent.

